1
00:00:00,131 --> 00:00:03,131
(Sheldon:)All right. There's no need to bark at me.

2
00:00:04,261 --> 00:00:07,351
(Sheldon:)According to the inexplicably
irritable nurse behind the desk...

3
00:00:07,514 --> 00:00:10,724
...you're after the man who claims
to be having a heart attack...

4
00:00:10,892 --> 00:00:14,102
(Sheldon:)...but appears to be well enough
to play Doodle Jump on his iPhone.

5
00:00:15,772 --> 00:00:18,192
(Sheldon:)We have to fill these out.

6
00:00:18,483 --> 00:00:20,653
"Describe illness or injury."

7
00:00:21,027 --> 00:00:23,317
(Penny:)I dislocated my shoulder.

8
00:00:23,488 --> 00:00:24,948
(Sheldon:)All right.

9
00:00:25,115 --> 00:00:27,705
And "how did the accident occur?"

10
00:00:27,868 --> 00:00:30,158
You already know that.

11
00:00:30,328 --> 00:00:34,378
Cause of accident:
lack of adhesive ducks.

12
00:00:37,544 --> 00:00:39,124
(Sheldon:)Okay, medical history.

13
00:00:39,296 --> 00:00:41,836
-Have you been diagnosed with diabetes?
-No.

14
00:00:42,007 --> 00:00:43,467
(Sheldon:)-Kidney disease?
-No.

15
00:00:43,633 --> 00:00:46,473
(Sheldon:)-Migraines?
-Getting one.

16
00:00:47,304 --> 00:00:49,184
(Sheldon:)-Are you currently pregnant?
-No.

17
00:00:49,347 --> 00:00:51,597
(Sheldon:)Are you sure? You look a bit puffy.

18
00:00:53,810 --> 00:00:56,690
Change migraine to "yes."

19
00:00:57,272 --> 00:01:00,772
-"When was your last menstrual period?"
-Oh, next question.

